    "The age runs from the proxy's upgrade to implementation 0x354cca2f, which the anchor's listToken ran. The BSC proxy 0xdac6ea96 runs the same implementation address; the attacker repeated the list-and-withdraw there minutes later, so those legs are campaign.",
    "All three tokens are thin (rule 12): the attacker's Ethereum STC swaps failed and its sales on both chains moved the price. Each token is valued at the attacker's realised average sale price (BNB or ETH proceeds at DefiLlama prices), applied to every unit taken on both chains, including units still held."
